# The wasm-opt arguments for every module this repository builds: the page's
# start module and the modules split from it, the bundles
# the app SDK writes, and the model module every app's package carries. One
# list, so the module a size check measures is the module a device runs.
#
# Read by crates/browser/tilo-browser-runtime/scripts/build.sh and
# tools/tilo-app-cli (embedded when it compiles, for the app's model
# module). A comment is a line starting with `#`; every other word is an
# argument.
-Oz
--enable-bulk-memory
--enable-nontrapping-float-to-int
# The modules are compiled with `+simd128` (.cargo/config.toml): binaryen
# refuses to read SIMD instructions it was not told to enable.
--enable-simd
# The split modules keep the name section the splitter read until it is gone
# with the rest of the debug information, and a producer section buys the page
# nothing.
--strip-debug
--strip-producers
# Sound for rustc's stack-first wasm32 layout: the first KiB is the bottom of
# the stack, reached only by a stack about to overflow.
--low-memory-unused
